      "post_date": "Mon May 04, 2020 4:42 pm",
      "post_datetime": "2020-05-04T21:42:29+00:00",
      "post_subject": "Geola polymer",
      "content_md": "yes, the mix of the R+G beams are more of a greenish yellow .. because it has a higher red sensitivity. the beams was spread with a fiber negative lens with the curved side toward the beams and the flat side toward the plate angle of the beam was about 30% to the plate. expose was about 5 mins. you can see visually the change in the polymer as you expose it. then set out in the sun to bleach out the dyes",
